  wModel: { title: 'a handover note', lines: [
    '**HANDOVER · Front desk and guest services · H. Alloush to R. Sabbagh · effective 12 November · read before our hour on Monday at 09.00**',
    '**HOW THIS NOTE IS ORGANISED, AND WHY.** **By decision, not by topic.** **The passwords, the rota, the supplier list and the standing orders are all in the shared folder and you can read them without me.** **What you cannot read is why eleven things are the way they are, and that is what follows: each with the date it was decided, the reason, and what would make it worth changing.** **The last part matters most. Without it you inherit eleven rules and no way out of any of them.**',
    '**THE DECISIONS, WITH THEIR CONDITIONS FOR REVISITING.** **Barada Travel is invoiced in advance: imposed July 2022 after two unpaid invoices; revisit if they are clean for eight consecutive quarters — they are at five.** **The night round goes to the basement before the upper floors: decided January 2024 after the panel fault; revisit when the addressable panel is commissioned, which is due 22 January.** **Nahas Systems was not renewed for maintenance: November 2024, after three call-outs took more than forty-eight hours; revisit if they change their service manager, which I am told is likely.** **Early check-in is free before 11.00 and charged after: May 2023, because the housekeeping overtime was running at 180,000 a month; revisit if the morning departure pattern changes.**',
    '**THE PEOPLE, AND I HAVE WRITTEN ONLY WHAT HAPPENS.** **The breakfast chef and the second commis cannot be rostered on the same early shift: service stopped twice in June when they were.** **The night porter will not telephone me after midnight unless told explicitly that he may, which is why the standing instruction says so in writing.** **Lama holds every agent relationship in her head and has never been asked to write any of it down; that is the next handover problem after this one and I have not solved it.** **Nothing else in this note is an opinion about anybody and you should not read one into it.**',
    '**WHAT IS ABOUT TO HAPPEN, WITH DATES.** **The Barada contract renews 1 March unless notice is given by 31 January.** **The addressable panel is installed 22 January and the licence exemption runs to 30 November next year; the committee wants a report at three months.** **The engineer’s lift report of March is superseded by the July one and is still in the file — I have marked it, and you should remove it rather than trust the marking.** **The laundry contract ends 30 April and should go out to two other firms this time.**',
    '**WHAT I GOT WRONG, IN MY OWN WORDS.** **I held the Haddad laundry contract a year longer than I should have, because changing it meant three weeks of work in a season and I kept finding reasons.** **It cost us about 400,000 and a complaint that reached the owners in August.** **I am writing it here because you will find it in the file within a month, and finding it from me tells you something about this note that finding it alone would not.**',
    '**AND HOW WE DO THIS ON MONDAY.** **Read the note first; then an hour with it open and you asking why.** **Forty pages are not a handover. The hour is the handover, and the note is only what makes the hour possible.** **Anything you ask that I cannot answer, I will write to you about by Friday, and I will keep my telephone answerable for a month after the twelfth.**' ] },
